def is_balanced(text):
    stack = []
    brackets = {'(': ')', '[': ']', '{': '}'}

    for char in text:
        if char in brackets:
            stack.append(char)
        elif stack and char == brackets[stack[-1]]:
            stack.pop()
        else:
            return False

    return len(stack) == 0
```

This code uses a stack to keep track of the opening brackets. It checks each character in the input string. If a closing bracket is encountered, it checks if the corresponding opening bracket is on the stack. If the stack is empty or the opening bracket doesn't match, it returns False. If the loop completes without popping anything, it means all opening brackets were matched, so the function returns True.
